{
    "pageid": 4899,
    "title": "Imperial elective",
    "sections": [
        {
            "heading": "Introduction",
            "level": 1,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Imperial elective is the succession law of the Byzantine Empire and Roman Empire, where the most prestigious and competent candidate is favored. Upon the reigning emperor's death, the candidate with the most points becomes the new emperor."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Features",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Only available to the Byzantine empire and Roman empire.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Locks itself in: A ruler with Imperial elective succession can only change succession indirectly (e.g. forced to Gavelkind by faction or in exchange for lifting excommunication ) or by obtaining another empire (e.g. with a claim or by re-creating the HRE by decision ) or if the title has special clause for republic elective",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "The emperor’s close family members (spouse included), any claimants to the title, the current Marshal , and any commander under the emperor, can all be nominated as successors.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "The emperor, all of his councillors , and all of his commanders are valid electors.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Commanders can no longer be unlanded, and must be vassals of at count tier.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Each elector's voting power scales based on their influence.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Electors will prefer to vote for a competent and prestigious successor.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "A powerful and influential emperor can push through his preferred candidate, even if most of the electors are against it. However, a weak and ineffective emperor will see his voting power decrease significantly.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "The only succession law whereby physical mutilation disqualifies candidates.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Enables Roman Imperial government .",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Mechanics",
            "level": 2,
            "content": []
        },
        {
            "heading": "Electors",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Valid electors are:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "The emperor.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "The emperor's councilors.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "The emperor's commanders.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Unlike other elective types, the ruler has to curry favor with the most powerful members of his court rather than his vassals."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Candidates",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Valid candidates are:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "The emperor's close family (including spouse).",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "The emperor's marshal.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "The emperor's commanders.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Title claimants.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Mutilated characters are disqualified."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Candidate appeal",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "The appeal of candidates is based on many factors, as detailed in the article Succession voting . Voters in Imperial Elective have additional preferences:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Prefer adults",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Prefer high-martial commanders and marshal",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "[Byzantine voters] Prefer Born in the Purple (Byzantine Empire only) or Despot",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "[Greek voters] Prefer high-intrigue councilors and minor title holders",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "[Roman voters] Prefer high-diplomacy councilors and minor title holders",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Disfigurement gets higher maluses",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Emperor's voting power",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Increased with:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Diplomacy skill",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Reduced with:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Not Born in the Purple (Byzantine empire only)",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Disfigurement (Byzantine empire only)",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Appointing a marshal or commander with below 10 martial skill, when another candidate has 5 higher martial skill",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Discharging a marshal or commander with 12+ martial skill, except when they are no longer eligible or when immediately moving them to another council or commander position",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
