        {
            "heading": "Strategies as emperor",
            "level": 2,
            "content": []
        },
        {
            "heading": "Ensure that most candidates are dynastic",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Imperial Elective lets you control who the candidates are. Take advantage of this to ensure your dynasty will not lose the election, even in situations where you can't control exactly who gets elected."
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Arrange matrilineal marriages for daughters to ensure grandchildren (future claimants) are dynastic.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Grant titles to kin , especially those with bloodlines that improve their combat prowess.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Take care when appointing commanders and marshal . Try to appoint either dynasty members or characters who can't or won't get votes (e.g. few positive traits, disfigured, female).",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Special vassals",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Certain vassals are disqualified from election, and can thus be appointed as commander or marshal without worry:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Create merchant republics . They will eventually have +2 martial from cellar buildings .",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Create count+ republics. Send your courtiers to be future mayors by matrilineally marrying them into the city.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Create count+ theocracies. Send your courtiers to be future priests using investiture (Catholic) or order to take the vows .",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Vassalize mercenaries and holy orders . Their leaders tend to be competent.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Note: the game has a certain issue by which you can ultimately bypass the 1/10th limit on vassal republics and theocracies. However, the doesn't recognize the limit, when you are ready to give unlanded characters potential republican/theocratic territories. By making a city or temple the top holding of the duchy (and giving out the castle, which you have replaced) and then awarding either the entire duchy or kingdom to an unlanded courtier, will automatically create, respectively, either a republic or theocracy. Therefore, ultimately you can have your entire Empire comprising of vassal Theocracies and Republics, so you will never have to worry about potential non-dynastic succession.\nThis has several downsides, however:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Republics are relatively impotent when defending their areas from raiders.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Vassal Republic and Theocracies provide less levies. However, since Imperial government allows you to hold cities too, you can get large amount of levies from your demesne, so this should not be a serious problem.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "This strategy will make every coastal duchy a Merchant Republic (Unless king-tier liege is also a MR, in which case, they will revert to ordinary republics). Increased competition will curb trade power of the patricians, consequently decreasing potential tax income from them.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Merchant Republics NEVER accept either title revocation or vassal retraction, meaning that you have to go to war in every case.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Ecumenical Patriarch is more reluctant to excommunicate priests (which includes rulers of theocracies, naturally).",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Honorary titles",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Bestow Byzantine honorary titles to influence the election:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Give Byzantine titles to dynastic candidates not on the council , so their political skill boosts their electability",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Give Byzantine titles to compliant voters to boost their voting power",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Despot counts the same as Born in the purple and can push a candidate ahead in a close race.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Strategies as the emperor's vassal",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Aim to be the Marshal or a commander : Securing eligibility is the first step.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Aim to serve on the council : Encourage your liege to appoint you by being competent, or with Conclave , by becoming a powerful vassal . Being on the council makes you an elector and improves your score for Greek and Roman voters. Depending on the position, it may also boost your prestige and keep you out of battles (if you were already a Commander).",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Be on good terms with the electors : Since opinion constitutes part of the points system.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Befriend the emperor : if you are nominated by the current ruler, other voters who like the emperor are likely to vote for you as well.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Avoid mutilation : Since it means permanent disqualification (barring supernatural interference). As a Marshal or commander, always be aware of your character's location so as to avoid as many battles as possible.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}